vanillic.en:
a. Pertaining to, or derived from, vanilla or vanillin;
   resembling vanillin; specifically, designating an alcohol and an acid
   respectively, vanillin being the intermediate aldehyde.

virulency.en:
n. The quality or state of being virulent or venomous;
   poisonousness; malignancy.
n. Extreme bitterness or malignity of disposition.

vitrescence.en:
n. The quality or state of being vitreous; glassiness, or
   the quality of being vitrescent; capability of conversion into glass;
   susceptibility of being formed into glass.

vocality.en:
n. The quality or state of being vocal; utterableness;
   resonance; as, the vocality of the letters.
n. The quality of being a vowel; vocalic character.

voluntariness.en:
n. The quality or state of being voluntary;
   spontaneousness; specifically, the quality or state of being free in
   the exercise of one's will.
